  "messages": [
    {
      "clusterLabel": 0,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.5539,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.5,
      "sequenceNumber": 1,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "The web app loads in 8 seconds and we need to get it under 2. Let's brainstorm all possible optimizations.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:00:05.000Z",
      "userId": "user_zara",
      "userName": "Zara"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 0,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.4091,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.6,
      "sequenceNumber": 2,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "Starting with the frontend — 3MB JavaScript bundle is huge. We need code splitting and tree shaking.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:00:22.000Z",
      "userId": "user_vik",
      "userName": "Vik"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": -1,
      "messageType": "disagreement",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.3615,
      "sentimentLabel": "negative",
      "sentimentScore": 0.375,
      "sequenceNumber": 3,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "Also lazy loading routes. Users shouldn't download the admin dashboard code when visiting the homepage.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:00:40.000Z",
      "userId": "user_maya",
      "userName": "Maya"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 0,
      "messageType": "question",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.6312,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.5,
      "sequenceNumber": 4,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "What about the images? 5MB of images is massive. WebP format can cut that by 50-60%.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:00:58.000Z",
      "userId": "user_arjun",
      "userName": "Arjun"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 0,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.3917,
      "sentimentLabel": "positive",
      "sentimentScore": 0.675,
      "sequenceNumber": 5,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "Good point. Plus responsive images with srcset — serve smaller images to mobile devices.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:01:15.000Z",
      "userId": "user_zara",
      "userName": "Zara"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": -1,
      "messageType": "new idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.4116,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.5417,
      "sequenceNumber": 6,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "Let me think about a different approach. What about server-side rendering? That would give instant first paint.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:01:35.000Z",
      "userId": "user_vik",
      "userName": "Vik"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 0,
      "messageType": "disagreement",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.341,
      "sentimentLabel": "positive",
      "sentimentScore": 0.85,
      "sequenceNumber": 7,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "SSR is good but it shifts the load to the server. With 15 API calls on page load, the server would need to handle all of those.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:01:55.000Z",
      "userId": "user_maya",
      "userName": "Maya"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 0,
      "messageType": "question",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.4391,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.5,
      "sequenceNumber": 8,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "What if we reduce those 15 API calls? Maybe aggregate them into 2-3 BFF (Backend for Frontend) endpoints.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:02:15.000Z",
      "userId": "user_arjun",
      "userName": "Arjun"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 0,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.4578,
      "sentimentLabel": "positive",
      "sentimentScore": 0.625,
      "sequenceNumber": 9,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "Or GraphQL! One query to fetch exactly what the page needs instead of 15 REST calls.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:02:35.000Z",
      "userId": "user_zara",
      "userName": "Zara"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 0,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.4996,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.6,
      "sequenceNumber": 10,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "GraphQL would solve the over-fetching problem too. REST endpoints return too much data we don't need.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:02:55.000Z",
      "userId": "user_vik",
      "userName": "Vik"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 0,
      "messageType": "new idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.4532,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.5,
      "sequenceNumber": 11,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "But GraphQL has a learning curve and adds complexity. Maybe BFF is simpler for now.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:03:15.000Z",
      "userId": "user_maya",
      "userName": "Maya"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 1,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.4904,
      "sentimentLabel": "positive",
      "sentimentScore": 0.7,
      "sequenceNumber": 12,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "Let's move to the backend. The 3-second database queries are a huge bottleneck. We need indexing.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:03:35.000Z",
      "userId": "user_arjun",
      "userName": "Arjun"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 1,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.7304,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.5875,
      "sequenceNumber": 13,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "Definitely indexing. But also query optimization. Use EXPLAIN to find full table scans and fix them.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:03:55.000Z",
      "userId": "user_zara",
      "userName": "Zara"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 1,
      "messageType": "question",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.5007,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.55,
      "sequenceNumber": 14,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "What about adding a caching layer? Redis for frequently accessed data. Cache invalidation on writes.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:04:15.000Z",
      "userId": "user_vik",
      "userName": "Vik"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 1,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.5394,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.5,
      "sequenceNumber": 15,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "Redis could cut DB load by 80%. Set TTL based on how often data changes. Product listings can be cached for 5 minutes.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:04:35.000Z",
      "userId": "user_maya",
      "userName": "Maya"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": -1,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.6735,
      "sentimentLabel": "positive",
      "sentimentScore": 0.75,
      "sequenceNumber": 16,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "Now let's think about infrastructure. CDN for static assets — images, JS, CSS all served from edge locations.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:04:55.000Z",
      "userId": "user_arjun",
      "userName": "Arjun"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": -1,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.3638,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.5,
      "sequenceNumber": 17,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "CloudFront or Cloudflare. Cache headers set properly. Immutable assets with content hash in filenames.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:05:15.000Z",
      "userId": "user_zara",
      "userName": "Zara"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": -1,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.554,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.4881,
      "sequenceNumber": 18,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "HTTP/2 multiplexing would help too. Multiple resources over single connection instead of 6 parallel connections.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:05:35.000Z",
      "userId": "user_vik",
      "userName": "Vik"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": -1,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.3744,
      "sentimentLabel": "positive",
      "sentimentScore": 0.75,
      "sequenceNumber": 19,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "Don't forget gzip or brotli compression. Brotli gives 20% better compression than gzip for text assets.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:05:55.000Z",
      "userId": "user_maya",
      "userName": "Maya"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 0,
      "messageType": "question",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.5871,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.5278,
      "sequenceNumber": 20,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "What about preloading critical resources? rel=preload for the main CSS and critical JS chunks.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:06:15.000Z",
      "userId": "user_arjun",
      "userName": "Arjun"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": -1,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.5831,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.55,
      "sequenceNumber": 21,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "And preconnect to third-party domains. If we have analytics, fonts, CDNs — DNS resolution happens early.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:06:35.000Z",
      "userId": "user_zara",
      "userName": "Zara"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": -1,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.3006,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.5,
      "sequenceNumber": 22,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "Service workers! Cache the app shell and critical data. The second visit would be instant.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:06:55.000Z",
      "userId": "user_vik",
      "userName": "Vik"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": -1,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.5268,
      "sentimentLabel": "positive",
      "sentimentScore": 0.6917,
      "sequenceNumber": 23,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "That's a PWA approach. Good for repeat visitors but doesn't help first load much.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:07:15.000Z",
      "userId": "user_maya",
      "userName": "Maya"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 0,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.5412,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.6,
      "sequenceNumber": 24,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "True. For first load, we should think about critical CSS — inline the above-the-fold styles.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:07:35.000Z",
      "userId": "user_arjun",
      "userName": "Arjun"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": -1,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.6651,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.5,
      "sequenceNumber": 25,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "Let me also suggest connection pooling for database. pg-pool or HikariCP depending on stack.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:07:55.000Z",
      "userId": "user_zara",
      "userName": "Zara"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": -1,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.5385,
      "sentimentLabel": "positive",
      "sentimentScore": 0.625,
      "sequenceNumber": 26,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "And N+1 query detection. ORMs love generating N+1 queries. Eager loading with proper joins.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:08:15.000Z",
      "userId": "user_vik",
      "userName": "Vik"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": -1,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.6231,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.4375,
      "sequenceNumber": 27,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "For images specifically, lazy loading with Intersection Observer API. Only load images as they scroll into view.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:08:35.000Z",
      "userId": "user_maya",
      "userName": "Maya"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": -1,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.5654,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.5875,
      "sequenceNumber": 28,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "Placeholder blur images too. Show a tiny blurred version while the full image loads. Like Medium does.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:08:55.000Z",
      "userId": "user_arjun",
      "userName": "Arjun"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": -1,
      "messageType": "question",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.5115,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.55,
      "sequenceNumber": 29,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "OK let's prioritize all these ideas. What gives us the biggest improvement with least effort?",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:09:15.000Z",
      "userId": "user_zara",
      "userName": "Zara"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 0,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.5709,
      "sentimentLabel": "positive",
      "sentimentScore": 0.8083,
      "sequenceNumber": 30,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "CDN plus compression is the quickest win. Just configuration changes, no code needed. Easily saves 2-3 seconds.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:09:35.000Z",
      "userId": "user_vik",
      "userName": "Vik"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 1,
      "messageType": "agreement",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.5024,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.5,
      "sequenceNumber": 31,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "Agreed. Then database indexing and Redis caching. That fixes the 3-second DB queries.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:09:55.000Z",
      "userId": "user_maya",
      "userName": "Maya"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 0,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.3372,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.5,
      "sequenceNumber": 32,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "Third priority: code splitting and image optimization. Reduces the 3MB JS and 5MB images.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:10:15.000Z",
      "userId": "user_arjun",
      "userName": "Arjun"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": 0,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.4287,
      "sentimentLabel": "neutral",
      "sentimentScore": 0.58,
      "sequenceNumber": 33,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "And consolidating API calls is medium effort, high impact. BFF approach rather than GraphQL for speed.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:10:35.000Z",
      "userId": "user_zara",
      "userName": "Zara"
    },
    {
      "clusterLabel": -1,
      "messageType": "building on idea",
      "messageTypeConfidence": 0.2424,
      "sentimentLabel": "positive",
      "sentimentScore": 0.6625,
      "sequenceNumber": 34,
      "source": "text",
      "text": "SSR and service workers are longer-term investments. Important but not the first thing to tackle.",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-15T18:10:55.000Z",
      "userId": "user_vik",
      "userName": "Vik"
    },
